  And yet turtles and snakes and fish just out of the egg can fend for
themselves.  Are you saying the are not babies?  The definition of baby in
English is:

: a very young child

: a very young animal

  (source m-w.com)

  All these case qualify.  I don't believe cifnu is that much different.
Words in brackets in the gismu list are rarely probative, and they
explanatory or expanding, rather than limiting, the definition. (Or are you
suggesting that "flira" means the same as "stedu" because it says "head" in
brackets?

                --gejyspa

